body: |-
  ## The arc (all on branch feat/memory-steward, part of unreleased 7.9.0)
  - **Phase A** (5ec2240a): premise-core `scanNativeMemory` + graph-validity (dead symbol = provably stale — the differentiator); CLI `paradigm memory review|prune|route|merge|pin`; advisory Stop-hook Check 15; self-clearing `advise` remediations. Bonus: fixed a latent premise-core type-export clean-build break. Owned by Loid, no new agent (TD-2026-06-14-467). Decision TD-2026-09-19-110.
  - **Phase B** (483c9ab3): B1 CLAUDE.md "Native Memory Hygiene" redirect (stops junk at source); B2 `paradigm memory sync` — advisory by default, strict demotion guards (never `##`/active-marked, only genuinely graph-stale leaf `###`+), `--write` (backup→atomic→verbatim→demote-not-delete→fail-open), opt-in compact `--projection`.
  - **Phase C** (64cd680b): Platform "Memory" section (ledger + sync-preview + one-click apply + visual "Apply sync") as a thin view over buildDigest/computeSync; C2a extracted return-shaped appliers (CLI byte-identical). Decision TD-2026-09-20-669.

  ## Two dogfood/review saves that shaped the design (the reusable lesson)
  1. Phase A dogfood on the real 57-entry dir: file-mention false positives (globs/prose-relative paths) were condemning good entries → symbols made the only prune authority; prune gated to status types.
  2. Phase B dry-run on a COPY of the real 18KB MEMORY.md: autonomous demotion flagged the "⭐ START HERE" Warpline arc + Release Conventions → reworked to advisory + strict guards (founder call). Green unit tests missed both; real-data dry-run caught them. RULE: for any tool transforming user-authored artifacts, dry-run against real data before trusting the suite.
  3. Phase C Aegis pass: HIGH platform-wide CSRF (ACAO:* + socket-bind-only ^local-only) — a browser page could POST to 127.0.0.1 and mutate ~/.claude. Fixed with request-time Host+Origin loopback enforcement (#local-guard); also closed the pre-existing tasks-write exposure.

  ## Non-negotiable principle held throughout
  Surface, human decides — NEVER auto-delete. "Lean" = dedup + demote-to-archive + human-gated prune. Real ~/.claude never touched during any dev/test (sandbox HOME + copies only).

  ## State / open
  - NOT pushed or published — founder runs `git push` + `npm publish` (7.9.0: paradigm 7.9.0, plugin.json 7.9.0, premise-core 3.9.0).
  - Follow-ups: T-2026-09-19-001 (.cursor hooks generator sync), T-2026-09-20-001 (sync backup rotation + preview/write TOCTOU, low).
  - Deferred: Phase C could gain live WS refresh (#memory-changed broadcast wired but UI not yet subscribing).
  - Still open from session start: the dev-education content series (Map/Compass/Journal spine) + felt-pains dump.
